      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 6. Train\n",
        "\n",
        "This is gradient descent, written out. It is the exact five-step loop from class:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Predict** with the current parameters\n",
        "2. **Measure the loss** — how wrong those predictions were\n",
        "3. Work out **which way is downhill** for every parameter\n",
        "4. Take a **small step** that way\n",
        "5. **Repeat**\n",
        "\n",
        "Watch the loss fall. That is the entire show."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-15",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-31T03:43:50.115706Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-31T03:43:50.115659Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-31T03:44:00.612352Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-31T03:44:00.611592Z"
        },
        "id": "cell-15",
        "outputId": "586fe8fa-60b5-4b8c-8185-9fcea9af238d",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "epoch   0   loss 2.303   train accuracy   9.9%   ##############################################\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "learning_rate = 0.5\n",
        "epochs = 300\n",
        "\n",
        "history = []\n",
        "for epoch in range(epochs + 1):\n",
        "    probs = softmax(X_train @ W + b)                                          # 1. predict\n",
        "    loss = -np.mean(np.log(probs[np.arange(len(y_train)), y_train] + 1e-9))   # 2. loss\n",
        "    grad = (probs - Y_train_onehot) / len(y_train)                            # 3. downhill\n",
        "    W -= learning_rate * (X_train.T @ grad)                                   # 4. step\n",
        "    b -= learning_rate * grad.sum(axis=0)                                     # 4. step\n",
        "                                                                              # 5. repeat\n",
        "    accuracy = (probs.argmax(axis=1) == y_train).mean()\n",
        "    history.append((loss, accuracy))\n",
        "    if epoch % 25 == 0:\n",
        "        bar = \"#\" * int(loss * 20)\n",
        "        print(f\"epoch {epoch:>3}   loss {loss:5.3f}   train accuracy {accuracy:6.1%}   {bar}\")"
      ]
    },
